// ?Rva00457090EmitBL@@YAXRAXDD0@Z
// partial score=0.68 date=2026-09-11
// The real callee is the already-pinned ?bfmeRunBL@@YAXPAXH0@Z at 0x0002126F
// (called x2, matching the brief), not an invented/unresolvable name: the
// prior 0.85 stash declared `extern "C" void bfmeSendCJ(...)`, which cannot
// resolve and, worse, is unreproducible -- probe.py measures the identical
// prior source at 35/66 diff today, not the claimed 9/66. This shape (twin
// of the landed BfmeConv1754.cpp bfmeSendBL, same idiom, no |0x40 term)
// reaches 45/66 (21 diff) as the best of several tried spellings.
// Residual: retail reloads the `target`/`extra` stack args from memory
// separately inside EACH arm (mov ecx,[esp+0x10]/mov edx,[esp+4] appear
// twice, once per arm, right after the `je`). MSVC 7.1 always hoists that
// pair of loads to one shared point between the second `test cl,cl` and the
// `je`, regardless of source spelling. Ruled out: plain parameters (35
// diff, loads hoisted before the flags computation too); `volatile`-casting
// only one of target/extra (still 35 diff -- both must be volatile together
// to reach 21); both parameters declared `void *volatile` (21 diff, the
// best); per-arm local copies of both under volatile parameters (identical
// 21 diff, no further change); `_ReadWriteBarrier()` before the `if` (worse,
// 31 diff, disturbs the already-matching flags prefix); `_ReadWriteBarrier()`
// inside each arm (no effect, load already hoisted before the barrier
// point); `// cl: /Og-` (much worse, 62 diff, reintroduces a full ebp frame
// and drops the sete/inc idiom). No clean C++ spelling forces the reload to
// sit after the `je`; the barrier would need to land between the branch's
// `test` and its `je`, which no C++ construct can target. t=35min
// model=Sonnet 5
